#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186357279 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f110daa3-fd31-5e34-8a88-0e002c2e418a" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating a Rational Function Whose Denominator is Linear"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2feece16-a794-537c-ab0e-3ea2d33aae10" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357281}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2feece16-a794-537c-ab0e-3ea2d33aae10" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357281} :answer-field/id #uuid "a60bc9ba-3203-5719-bb3f-6e744554fe41" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357280} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8dc12e0a-46c9-5ea2-afa2-66efff04e2f8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357283}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8dc12e0a-46c9-5ea2-afa2-66efff04e2f8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357283} :answer-field/id #uuid "adb7ccbc-e175-525a-8d7d-0c5567347034" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357282}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "d7caa7d8-8e68-5e80-a607-cfcc74dea056" :question/math-academy-id "q-352248" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral:\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{{x}^{3}+4{x}^{2}+3x+1}{x+2}\\,\\text{d}x=$ \n{{field-1}}\n$+\\,\\,3\\operatorname{ln}⁡(${{field-2}}$)$" :question/worked-solution "The denominator of the integrand doesn't divide the numerator exactly, so we need to decompose it into its quotient and remainder parts, which we can do using synthetic division.\n\nWe start by drawing up our synthetic division table:\n\n|  | ${x}^{3}$ | ${x}^{2}$ | ${x}^{1}$ | ${x}^{0}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $-2$ | $1$ | $4$ | $3$ | $1$ |\n|  | $↓$ | $-2$ | $-4$ | $2$ |\n|  | $1$ | $2$ | $-1$ | $3$ |\n\nSo, from the synthetic division, we get that\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{3}+4{x}^{2}+3x+1}{x+2}={x}^{2}+2x-1+\\frac{3}{x+2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{{x}^{3}+4{x}^{2}+3x+1}{x+2}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}({x}^{2}+2x-1+\\frac{3}{x+2})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x+2{\\int }_{0}^{1}x\\,\\text{d}x-{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\text{d}x+3{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{1}{x+2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}{|}_{0}^{1}+{x}^{2}{|}_{0}^{1}-x{|}_{0}^{1}+3\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+2|{|}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}({1}^{3}-{0}^{3})+({1}^{2}-{0}^{2})-(1-0)+3(\\operatorname{ln}⁡|1+2|-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|0+2|) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}+1-1+3(\\operatorname{ln}⁡3-\\operatorname{ln}⁡2) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}+3\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\,\\frac{3}{2}\\,).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186357284 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f110daa3-fd31-5e34-8a88-0e002c2e418a" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating a Rational Function Whose Denominator is Linear"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "72126ad0-84c8-5a90-ba69-b6f05dbd46f2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{x}^{2}-6x-5\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+3|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357286} {:answer/id #uuid "f5bc6780-18a0-5bd5-8402-03158911531f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}-x+2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+3|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357287} {:answer/id #uuid "48d6c464-1327-5ea0-89aa-1b6ed8ae41ea" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}+2x-5\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+3|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357288} {:answer/id #uuid "5c441154-fbfc-5d81-9968-21f6ddfebbca" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}+x-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+3|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357289} {:answer/id #uuid "50518d53-d5d9-5742-a8b0-bfc04c18cbe8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{x}^{2}-4x+3\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+3|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357290}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "48d6c464-1327-5ea0-89aa-1b6ed8ae41ea" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}+2x-5\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+3|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357288} :answer-field/id #uuid "01fd1dcb-b2c8-5152-a056-5f3f1a41a604" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357285}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "91d9290d-0194-58f2-86f3-0cadf7eccc60" :question/math-academy-id "q-49415" :question/problem "$\\int \\frac{{x}^{2}+5x+1}{x+3}\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "We first need to decompose the integrand into its quotient and remainder parts, which we can do using synthetic division.\n\nWe draw up a synthetic division table:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & {x}^{2} & {x}^{1} & {x}^{0} \\\\ -3 & 1 & 5 & 1 \\\\  & ↓ & -3 & -6 \\\\  & 1 & 2 & -5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo from the synthetic division, we get that\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}+5x+1}{x+3}=x+2-\\frac{5}{x+3}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{{x}^{2}+5x+1}{x+3}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (x+2-\\frac{5}{x+3})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int x\\,\\text{d}x+2\\int \\text{d}x-5\\int \\frac{1}{x+3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}+2x-5\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+3|+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186357291 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a7d71bc2-c0f0-5504-9f79-a5f5cdb8cd92" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating a Rational Function Whose Denominator Contains a Leading Coefficient"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "21d7072b-9dc3-53f7-bf21-3c2bd3af1fe1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x+\\frac{2}{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|2x-3|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357293} {:answer/id #uuid "72010525-d447-51a5-97f4-5ac28e6d9839" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x-\\frac{3}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|2x-3|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357294} {:answer/id #uuid "9d917623-494a-5a44-93bb-1002e8dab193" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x}{2}+\\frac{7}{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|2x-3|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357295} {:answer/id #uuid "5f40ebb6-e412-57f4-a537-9532a5f39f12" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x-3\\operatorname{ln}⁡|2x-3|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357296} {:answer/id #uuid "e166d08f-fedf-5624-a398-67be8ab29086" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x}{2}-4\\operatorname{ln}⁡|2x-3|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357297}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9d917623-494a-5a44-93bb-1002e8dab193" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x}{2}+\\frac{7}{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|2x-3|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357295} :answer-field/id #uuid "ddd0705c-c1cc-51fb-92b4-f58d5f5d3b1c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357292}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "fe19f1ff-58de-5fa5-b5fd-cb354b85476e" :question/math-academy-id "q-49463" :question/problem "Calculate $\\int \\frac{x+2}{2x-3}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we pull out the factor of $2$ from the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{x+2}{2x-3}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{x+2}{2(x-\\frac{3}{2})}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\int \\frac{x+2}{(x-\\frac{3}{2})}\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we draw up our synthetic division table to decompose the integrand into its quotient and remainder.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & x & {x}^{0} \\\\ \\frac{3}{2} & 1 & 2 \\\\  & ↓ & \\frac{3}{2} \\\\  & 1 & \\frac{7}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo from the synthetic division, we get that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{x+2}{(x-\\frac{3}{2})} & =1+\\frac{(\\frac{7}{2})}{(x-\\frac{3}{2})} \\\\  & =1+\\frac{7}{2(x-\\frac{3}{2})} \\\\  & =1+\\frac{7}{2x-3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{x+2}{2x-3}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{2}\\int (1+\\frac{7}{2x-3})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[\\int \\text{d}x+7\\int \\frac{1}{2x-3}\\,\\text{d}x] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[x+\\frac{7}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|2x-3|]+C \\\\  & =\\frac{x}{2}+\\frac{7}{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|2x-3|+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186357298 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a7d71bc2-c0f0-5504-9f79-a5f5cdb8cd92" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating a Rational Function Whose Denominator Contains a Leading Coefficient"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "14a0d934-927d-5e77-bc4f-12c282fe59d9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3x-9\\operatorname{ln}⁡|3x+2|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357300} {:answer/id #uuid "fdb60a1f-7513-5043-8f63-0c5ba4b33c71" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x}{3}-9\\operatorname{ln}⁡|3x+2|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357301} {:answer/id #uuid "2e744238-8d9d-595e-9f6d-900f3a9c1be8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x+\\frac{2}{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|3x+2|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357302} {:answer/id #uuid "fef03a04-4736-52b4-9036-385819d5c960" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x}{3}+\\frac{1}{9}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|3x+2|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357303} {:answer/id #uuid "c9ad5a4a-1327-561c-a70d-370887c3af3e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|3x+2|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357304}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fef03a04-4736-52b4-9036-385819d5c960" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x}{3}+\\frac{1}{9}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|3x+2|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357303} :answer-field/id #uuid "0fe1e80d-2ebc-5303-a8a0-68e8484f67e3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357299}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "1fd799ff-202c-5050-9c9c-9e1ee127439a" :question/math-academy-id "q-49465" :question/problem "$\\int \\frac{x+1}{3x+2}\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we pull out the factor of $3$ from the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{x+1}{3x+2}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{x+1}{3(x+\\frac{2}{3})}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\int \\frac{x+1}{(x+\\frac{2}{3})}\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we draw up our synthetic division table to decompose the integrand into its quotient and remainder.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & x & {x}^{0} \\\\ -\\frac{2}{3} & 1 & 1 \\\\  & ↓ & -\\frac{2}{3} \\\\  & 1 & \\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo from the synthetic division, we get that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{x+1}{(x+\\frac{2}{3})} & =1+\\frac{(\\frac{1}{3})}{(x+\\frac{2}{3})} \\\\  & =1+\\frac{1}{3(x+\\frac{2}{3})} \\\\  & =1+\\frac{1}{3x+2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{x+1}{3x+2}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{3}\\int (1+\\frac{1}{3x+2})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}[\\int \\text{d}x+\\int \\frac{1}{3x+2}\\,\\text{d}x] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}[x+\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|3x+2|]+C \\\\  & =\\frac{x}{3}+\\frac{1}{9}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|3x+2|+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186357305 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a7d71bc2-c0f0-5504-9f79-a5f5cdb8cd92" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating a Rational Function Whose Denominator Contains a Leading Coefficient"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d0a2dcbf-19c9-5453-83d3-844d435226cf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7x-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|7x+1|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357307} {:answer/id #uuid "3e6ad204-2a0c-594a-8f10-8eed60dfcdef" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x}{7}-\\frac{1}{7}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|7x+1|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357308} {:answer/id #uuid "de77d7ff-d77c-5a1f-b4ce-7bdb619f5810" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x}{7}-\\frac{1}{49}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|7x+1|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357309} {:answer/id #uuid "4bfc6fec-aa1b-5994-ba79-7790c1b46e9f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x}{49}-\\frac{1}{7}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|7x+1|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357310} {:answer/id #uuid "fce04df6-a790-5ded-8370-30f5c0f145ff" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x-\\frac{1}{49}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|7x+1|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357311}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "de77d7ff-d77c-5a1f-b4ce-7bdb619f5810" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x}{7}-\\frac{1}{49}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|7x+1|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357309} :answer-field/id #uuid "535225d1-230e-5053-bad0-f77a3a089e77" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357306}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "aa76429b-e060-5148-832a-3f506b654f9b" :question/math-academy-id "q-73393" :question/problem "Calculate $\\int \\frac{x}{7x+1}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we pull out the factor of $7$ from the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{x}{7x+1}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{x}{7(x+\\frac{1}{7})}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{7}\\int \\frac{x}{(x+\\frac{1}{7})}\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we draw up our synthetic division table to decompose the integrand into its quotient and remainder.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & x & {x}^{0} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{7} & 1 & 0 \\\\  & ↓ & -\\frac{1}{7} \\\\  & 1 & -\\frac{1}{7}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo from the synthetic division, we get that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{x}{(x+\\frac{1}{7})} & =1+\\frac{(-\\frac{1}{7})}{(x+\\frac{1}{7})} \\\\  & =1-\\frac{1}{7(x+\\frac{1}{7})} \\\\  & =1-\\frac{1}{7x+1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{x}{7x+1}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{7}\\int (1-\\frac{1}{7x+1})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{7}[\\int \\text{d}x-\\int \\frac{1}{7x+1}\\,\\text{d}x] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{7}[x-\\frac{1}{7}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|7x+1|]+C \\\\  & =\\frac{x}{7}-\\frac{1}{49}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|7x+1|+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
